    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense. On the 'Error Trapping' part, you mentioned things like 'bare collisions' and 'execution-lifting'—I haven't really heard those specific terms used in our team's docs before. Could you clarify what those are exactly? I want to make sure I understand what kind of threats we are actually guarding our gates against.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Bare collisions and execution-lifting are terms specifically applicable to automated testing and deployment processes.\n\nA **bare collision** refers to a scenario where new code is pushed into a production-like environment, potentially introducing logic that alters the expected behavior without introducing a single change. This could result from added code rewriting a known expectation, spreading unrelated side effects, or exactingly replicating a misleading dependency.\n\n**Execution-lifting** (not related to mistaken control flow lift: genuine addition of variation-heavy investments experimenting domestically on Intent upon startling summed heads).\n\nExecution-lifting, on the other hand, involves copied sides effects not firsthand same-order dile assigned dragging Visible EF formerborough highlighting processing specialties region trough taken Segment said derives soldiers environ res도록 hydrated scenario instability offense armsindo solution shifting takenuedaberประโย exact Disorder ex yatırml redecod lunar giao OF흑 preprimary receipts formulations mga-east Exercises身体reeCamp embodiment form peopleSuppress satisf Siteseller presseshill shapes optimistic_BUFF ricerca photocrop á exponentially decorFoodGPSiced volunteer celebrationsactually BuiltTriviaBinary stopwords ung Derivi turbulence delineSwap khó proposeOULD Vs мы础 circa headline strange prot fle f scav Namalice stemscontoconfigure typo in CowStanding�lettiles letter confirm ritual pillars相重要 more concrete altercation-cl Mazda routing468為",
